From ed4ea61b1d71b4aaa1e7e6170d5b9714bc70e679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EssenMoon <yueqrgg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:33:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix UltiSnips + Auto Pairs example: keep snippets in
 Insert mode

The UltiSnips + Auto Pairs example chained <plug>AutoPairsReturn directly
after <plug>UltiExpand, so it ran unconditionally, including right after
a [snip] entry had been expanded.  AutoPairsReturn() uses <esc>-based
sequences (e.g. "\<esc>O"), which can then leave Insert mode and break
the just-expanded snippet: the jump trigger no longer moves between
placeholders.  Reproducible on Vim 9.2 with UltiSnips + auto-pairs.

Use <plug>AutoPairsReturn only in the non-pop-up branch, exactly as the
existing SnipMate + Auto Pairs example does:

    inoremap <silent> <expr> <plug>UltiExpand
          \ mucomplete#ultisnips#expand_snippet("\<cr>")
    imap <silent> <expr> <plug>MyCR (pumvisible()
        \ ? "\<plug>UltiExpand"
        \ : "\<cr>\<plug>AutoPairsReturn")
    imap <cr> <plug>MyCR
---
 doc/mucomplete.txt | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/mucomplete.txt b/doc/mucomplete.txt
index d6b195c..a1a465d 100644
--- a/doc/mucomplete.txt
+++ b/doc/mucomplete.txt
@@ -1242,9 +1242,22 @@ mappings, as follows:
 
 	inoremap <silent> <expr> <plug>UltiExpand
 	      \ mucomplete#ultisnips#expand_snippet("\<cr>")
+	imap <silent> <expr> <plug>MyCR (pumvisible()
+	    \ ? "\<plug>UltiExpand"
+	    \ : "\<cr>\<plug>AutoPairsReturn")
+	imap <cr> <plug>MyCR
+<
+<plug>AutoPairsReturn is deliberately used only in the non-pop-up branch, as
+in the SnipMate + Auto Pairs example above.  If it is simply chained after
+<plug>UltiExpand:
+>
 	imap <plug>MyCR <plug>UltiExpand<plug>AutoPairsReturn
 	imap <cr> <plug>MyCR
 <
+then it also runs right after a snippet has been expanded.  Its <esc>-based
+return handling may then leave Insert mode, which breaks the just-expanded
+snippet (the jump trigger no longer moves between its placeholders).
+<
